  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The tool's indicators and reference values are specifically calibrated for an Algerian Mediterranean urban context, which may limit its direct applicability to different climate zones or urban structures without recalibration.",
      "what": "The study introduces HResRPS, an operational tool designed to evaluate and improve heatwave resilience in recreational public spaces. Developed and tested in the Mediterranean city of Jijel, Algeria, the framework structures resilience across three phases, eight attribute clusters, and 22 operational indicators using deep learning-based semantic clustering and a multidisciplinary Delphi-AHP process.",
      "why": "It provides urban planners and designers with concrete reference values and a composite index to diagnose specific spatial weaknesses and integrate heat-resilience criteria directly into the early stages of new urban design projects."
